 Prices are integer cents everywhere. Run the tests with `npm test`.
 
+## Monthly export
+
+`orders.exportMonth(month)` gives the orders placed in a month, as CSV text for the accountant's spreadsheet. The
+month is `YYYY-MM`; the text has a header line and then one line per order, by order number, with the columns
+`order`, `date` (as the order stores it), `customer` (the name) and `total` (what the customer pays, in euros with two
+decimals). Customers' email addresses and phone numbers are not exported. A value containing a comma or a quote is
+quoted, and a quote inside it is doubled. A month with no orders gives the header line alone, and a month that is not
+`YYYY-MM` is refused.
+
 ## Discount codes
 
 A customer can give an order one discount code with `orders.applyCode(orderNumber, code)`. A second code replaces
